      "text": "First, we expand the product $(3x^2 - 5x + 4)(7 - 2x)$ using the distributive property.\n\n\\[\n(3x^2 - 5x + 4)(7 - 2x) = 3x^2(7 - 2x) - 5x(7 - 2x) + 4(7 - 2x).\n\\]\n\nNext, we distribute each term within the parentheses:\n\n\\[\n= 3x^2 \\cdot 7 - 3x^2 \\cdot 2x - 5x \\cdot 7 + 5x \\cdot 2x + 4 \\cdot 7 - 4 \\cdot 2x.\n\\]\n\nSimplifying each term, we get:\n\n\\[\n= 21x^2 - 6x^3 - 35x + 10x^2 + 28 - 8x.\n\\]\n\nCombining like terms, we obtain:\n\n\\[\n= -6x^3 + (21x^2 + 10x^2) + (-35x - 8x) + 28.\n\\]\n\nSimplifying further:\n\n\\[\n= -6x^3 + 31x^2 - 43x + 28.\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the coefficients for the polynomial are $a = -6$, $b = 31$, $c = -43$, and $d = 28$.\n\nFinally, we calculate $8a + 4b + 2c + d$:\n\n\\[\n8a + 4b + 2c + d = 8(-6) + 4(31) + 2(-43) + 28.\n\\]\n\nSimplifying the expression, we get:\n\n\\[\n= -48 + 124 - 86 + 28.\n\\]\n\nTherefore:\n\n\\[\n= 28.\n\\]\n\nThus, the final answer is $\\boxed{28}$.",
